{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.NatInt","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Summable","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.faddeevPhi_phiBProd_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.faddeevPhi_phiBProd_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L398-L408","doc":"**The unconditional physical instance.**  At the substrate b-map\n`substrateB t` (`t = ln q₀ > 0`), `phiBProd` satisfies every `FaddeevPhi`\naxiom with no remaining hypotheses — the conjecture-class is a theorem-class\non the physical branch.  What stays open is only the `|q| = 1` fibre regime\n(real `b`), where the product diverges and the contour integral is the sole\ndefinition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.multipliable_denFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.multipliable_denFactor","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L369-L396","doc":"The denominator (modular-dual) family is multipliable whenever\n`Im b² > 0` (there `Re(−2πi/b²) < 0` as well — the `q̃` suppression). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.multipliable_numFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.multipliable_numFactor","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L343-L367","doc":"The numerator family is multipliable whenever `Im b² > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB_sq_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB_sq_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L312-L319","doc":"`Im (substrateB t)² > 0` for `t > 0` — the physical b-map sits on the\nproduct-supported (`Im b² > 0`) branch, where `phiBProd` realizes `Φ_b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB_sq","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L288-L310","doc":"`(substrateB t)² = (t/2π)·i` — the square is purely imaginary with\npositive imaginary part (for `t > 0`), i.e. `q = e^{2πib²} = e^{-t} = 1/q₀`\nand the product-branch condition `Im b² > 0` holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB_re_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB_re_pos","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L279-L286","doc":"`Re (substrateB t) > 0` for `t > 0` — the `FaddeevPhi.hb` precondition\nholds at the physical map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB","kind":"def","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L275-L277","doc":"The substrate b-map `b(t) = √(t/2π)·e^{iπ/4}` (`t = ln q₀`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.faddeevPhi_phiBProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.faddeevPhi_phiBProd","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L233-L263","doc":"**`phiBProd` inhabits `FaddeevPhi`** (given the two analytic convergence\nfacts as explicit hypotheses — see the module docstring).  This turns the\nconjecture-class into a theorem-class on the product-supported branch: the\nopen content that remains is (a) the `Multipliable` discharge (geometric\nbounds, `Im b² > 0`) and (b) the `|q| = 1` fibre regime, where the product\ndiverges and only the contour integral defines `Φ_b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.tprod_den_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.tprod_den_shift","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L213-L229","doc":"Denominator telescoping under the `1/b`-shift: the `+i/(2b)` product\ncarries the extra dual prefactor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.tprod_num_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.tprod_num_shift","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L195-L211","doc":"Numerator telescoping under the `b`-shift: the `−ib/2` product carries one\nextra factor — exactly the shift prefactor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denEven_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denEven_zero","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L186-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denFactor_shift_up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denFactor_shift_up","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L179-L184","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denFactor_shift_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denFactor_shift_down","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L171-L177","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numFactor_shift_binv_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numFactor_shift_binv_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L153-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denFactor_shift_b_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denFactor_shift_b_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L135-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numEven_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numEven_zero","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L128-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numFactor_shift_up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numFactor_shift_up","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L121-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numFactor_shift_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numFactor_shift_down","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L116-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.tprod_eq_zero_mul_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.tprod_eq_zero_mul_succ","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L94-L110","doc":"Split off the `k = 0` factor of a `tprod` over `ℕ`, assuming the shifted\ntail is multipliable (monoid-level replacement for `tprod_eq_zero_mul`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.succEquivCompl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.succEquivCompl","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L84-L92","doc":"`ℕ ≃ ({0}ᶜ : Set ℕ)` by `k ↦ k + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.phiBProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.phiBProd","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L70-L73","doc":"**The modular-double product.**  On `Im b² > 0` both halves converge\ngeometrically and this equals the Faddeev contour integral (battery S5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denEven","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L64-L68","doc":"Even-exponent dual variant `1 + q̃^{2k}·e^{2πz/b}`; its `k = 0` term is the\ndual shift prefactor `1 + e^{2πz/b}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.denFactor","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L58-L62","doc":"Denominator (modular-dual-half) factor `1 + q̃^{2k+1}·e^{2πz/b}`,\n`q̃ = e^{-iπ/b²}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numEven","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L52-L56","doc":"Even-exponent variant `1 + q^{2k}·e^{2πbz}` — the numerator family after a\n`−ib/2` shift of `z`; its `k = 0` term is the shift prefactor `1 + e^{2πbz}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.numFactor","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBProd.lean#L46-L50","doc":"Numerator (compact-half) factor `1 + q^{2k+1}·e^{2πbz}`, `q = e^{iπb²}`,\nwritten additively in the exponent. ","signatureChunk":0}]}